    "note": [
      "This pin records what render-oss/render-mcp-server ACTUALLY registers, captured by",
      "driving the built server through the MCP stdio handshake and reading its own",
      "tools/list -- not by regex over its source. Descriptions and annotations are",
      "deliberately excluded: they drift editorially and would fire the drift check on",
      "non-contractual churn. Only tool names and argument names are contractual here.",
      "",
      "Pinned to main, not to the latest release, deliberately. v0.3.0 (2026-01-14) is 83",
      "commits behind and still exposes update_cron_job, update_static_site and",
      "update_web_service -- placeholder tools that returned a dashboard link instead of",
      "updating anything. Upstream removed all three in b5f93eb (#89, 2026-07-23,",
      "'stop exposing placeholder update tools that only return dashboard links'), so",
      "pinning the release would enshrine a contract Render has explicitly repudiated.",
      "main additionally added trigger_deploy since v0.3.0.",
      "",
      "The drift check compares the 'tools' array only, so refreshing this file's 'pin'",
      "or 'source' metadata never registers as surface drift. Regenerate the comparable",
      "half with: scripts/render-mcp-capture.py --ref <commit> --tools-only"
    ]
  },
